Programs of the account's own
06-administrator-commands
Off as delivered. When you turn it on, the account's home screen gets a group My programs, and the person can add their own programs to it with the my.menu verb: a label, and the command they would type at their prompt.
A program added this way runs exactly as if the person had typed it, so it adds no access: the account's own switches apply. The person manages only their own list, never the standard tiles.
Turning it off hides the group and stops my.menu; the list stays in the account's file. The command it runs is set.pins with on or off.
